School Gardens
The WFP Centre of Excellence provided technical support for the publication “School gardens in the environmental, social and governance agenda of municipalities”, as result of a partnership between the Municipal Secretariat of Education Food Bank and the Department of Food and Nutrition Security of the city of Osasco/São Paulo, the Pé de Feijão Association, the NGO Prato Verde, and iFood. The manual provides support and guidance to public and private managers on:
• the relevance of school gardens and their
influence on the pedagogical process;
• raising financial support;
• the role of vegetable gardens for sustainability
and compliance with the UN Sustainable
Development Goals;
• guidance on implementation;
• budgetary benefits of vegetable gardens.
